<title>USA: Tegal to cut global workforce.</title>
<headline>Tegal to cut global workforce.</headline>
<dateline>PETALUMA, Calif. 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tegal Corp said it would reduce its global workforce by 12 percent.</p>
<p>The company said that the semiconductor capital equipment industry experienced a slowdown of orders due to excess capacity.</p>
<p>As a result, Tegal agreed to adjust its employment to its current level of business. The company expects quarter to quarter revenues and earnings to decline below current analyst estimates, beginning this quarter, and that these declines will be commensurate with what is happening in the industry as a whole. -- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
</text>
